{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Working Hard"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Homework Done"}, {"type": "position", "content": 7}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "isolation"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the \u200bcondition of being \u200balone, \u200bespecially when this makes you \u200bfeel \u200bunhappy"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I don't work well in isolation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about work responsibilities."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reckon"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bthink or \u200bbelieve"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I reckon I've been most productive in quiet places."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to come along"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to progress"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How are things coming along?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "significant"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "important"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Nothing really significant yet. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to hold up"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to delay"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you are late, it holds up the whole production schedule."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to forge ahead "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to \u200bsuddenly make a lot of \u200bprogress with something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: As soon as I finish this chapter, I'll forge ahead with the the next one."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "shortly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "soon"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  I'll finish up the editing shortly and then I can begin the layout whenever you want."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn10le09ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn10le09ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "  Adverbial Clauses"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " An adverbial clause is a group of words which plays the role of an adverb. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "(adverbial clause)In the examples above, the normal adverb and adverbial clause both tell us when the gong is to be hit. They are both adverbs of time. All adverbs (including adverbial clauses) can usually be categorized as one of the following:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Adverbs of Time</span><br/> An adverb of time states when something happens or how often. An adverb of time often starts with one of the following <span class=\"underline\">subordinating conjunctions</span>: <span class=\"italic\">after</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as long as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">as soon as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">before</span>, <span class=\"italic\">no sooner than</span>, <span class=\"italic\">since</span>, <span class=\"italic\">until</span>, <span class=\"italic\">when</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">while</span>. Here are some examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>After the game has finished, the king and pawn go into the same box. (Italian Proverb) <li>I stopped believing in Santa Claus when my mother took me to see him in a department store, and he asked for my autograph. (Shirley Temple) <li>As soon as you trust yourself, you will know how to live. (Johann Wolfgang von Goethe)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbs of Place</span><br/> An adverb of place states where something happens. An adverb of place often starts with a preposition (e.g., <span class=\"italic\">in</span>, <span class=\"italic\">on</span>, <span class=\"italic\">near</span>) or one of the following subordinating conjunctions: <span class=\"italic\">anywhere</span>, <span class=\"italic\">everywhere</span>, <span class=\"italic\">where</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">wherever</span>. Here are some examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>In a world where there is so much to be done, I felt strongly impressed that there must be something for me to do. (Dorothea Dix) <li>I am not afraid of the pen, the scaffold, or the sword. I will tell the truth wherever I please. (Mother Jones)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Adverbs of Manner</span><br/> An adverb of manner states how something is done. An adverb of manner often starts with one of the following subordinating conjunctions: <span class=\"italic\">as</span>, <span class=\"italic\">like</span>, or <span class=\"italic\">the way</span>. Here are some examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<ul><li>He acts like it is a joke. <li>We don't have conversations. You talk at me the way a teacher talks to a naughty student. <li>Except for an occasional heart attack, I feel as young as I ever did. (Robert Benchley)</li></ul>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "As soon as I finish this chapter, I'll forge ahead with the the next one."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I'd like to keep working on this chapter until it's perfect."}, {"type": "example", "content": "And you know that you can work on the editing anywhere you want, right?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You have to finish it as soon as possible."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I can begin the layout whenever you want."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Present Perfect with Report or Comment Phrases"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about past events that have a connection to the future. <br/> You can use the Present Perfect tense with other verbs to report or comment on events."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use verbs such as <span class=\"italic\">reckon, understand, suppose, guess</span> and <span class=\"italic\">imagine</span> to communicate your thoughts and to report about something that happened in the past and has a connection to the present. <br/><br/> The structure is:<br/><br/> subject + report/comment verb+ (that) + Present Perfect<br/><br/> For example:<br/><br/> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">understand (that) you have done</span> a lot of editing in previous jobs.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I understand that you have done a lot of editing in previous jobs."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I suppose that I have worked on several different documents in the past."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I reckon I've been most productive in quiet places but I do like to have people around."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I guess I've always worked best with the energy of being around people. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I imagine that you have chased lots of copy editors for their work."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, brainstorm adjectives to describe good and bad qualities in a manager."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of things that a good manager should and shouldn't do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write a paragraph describing the personality and behavior of a good manager."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Exchange paragraphs with another group and see if you had any of the same ideas."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I brainstorm qualities of a good manager."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I list things a manager should and shouldn't do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a paragraph describing a good manager."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I compare my paragraph with another group."}]}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"_data": [], "template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"id": 1, "type": "audio", "title": "", "_data": [], "template_override": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"audiosrc": "engenn10le09ob07re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn10le09ob07re2img05.jpg", "images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": "engenn10le09ob07re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Hi Kristi! How are things coming along?<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Great! As soon as I finish this chapter, I'll forge ahead with the next one. I'd like to keep working on this chapter until it's perfect.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>:  I understand that you have done a lot of editing in previous jobs. You must be pretty good at it.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I suppose that I have worked on several different documents in the past. Nothing really significant yet.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": "engenn10le09ob07re2img05.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Well, you'll get lots of experience here! And you know that you can work on the editing anywhere you want, right? We don't really have assigned work spaces here. Just find a spot where you are comfortable. And productive!<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: I reckon I've been most productive in quiet places but I do like to have people around. I don't work well in isolation. I guess I've always worked best with the energy of being around people.\n</br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: Okay. Well, that editing needs to be done by tomorrow so you have to finish it as soon as possible. It can't be late. If you are late, it holds up the whole production schedule.", "id": 2, "time": "21000", "image": "engenn10le09ob07re2img06.jpg"}, {"text": "<span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Okay, I will make this a priority and really focus on it. I imagine that you have chased lots of editorial assistants for their work. I don't want to waste anyone's time.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: So tomorrow will you be ready to work on some layout? We need to get going on that.<br><span class=\"strong\">Kristi</span>: Yes. I'll finish up the editing shortly and then I can begin the layout whenever you want.<br><span class=\"strong\">Boris</span>: That's great Kristi. I'm glad you're working with us. I think you've been a great addition to the team already.", "id": 3, "time": "56500", "image": "engenn10le09ob07re2img07.jpg"}]}}]}], "exercises": [{"questions": [], "stimuli_ids": [0], "id": 0, "type": "WLC", "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about solving problems."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can report facts about events or actions."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": " I can talk about my work responsibilities."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " What are the conditions in which you feel you are most productive?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": " Do you enjoy working when there are other people around or do you prefer to work alone? Why?"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}]}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", 